=== Signed relation-packet budget scout ===
source: HYP-2645 finite x-cell / Poisson-theta table
packet                 R6_box2  corr       corr/R6     density_vs_AP  coherence   route
AP_core                    982  0.302731  0.00030828      1.000000   0.009661  finite AP / bounded-core certificate
near_AP                    924  0.183854  0.00019898      0.940937   0.006048  signed wall transport / Freiman pocket
odd_AP                     546  0.213476  0.00039098      0.556008   0.009136  odd-sector owner/current sidecar
primes_ish                 414  0.009649  0.00002331      0.421589   0.000474  wide finite-cell / Poisson-theta route
squares_sidon              156  0.000536  0.00000344      0.158859   0.000043  wide/Sidon fast signed convergence

Interpretation:
- Raw relation density is not a theorem currency: odd_AP has fewer R6
  relations than near_AP but larger signed correction.
- Wide/Sidon packets have tiny signed activities and should be routed
  through finite-cell / Poisson-theta control, not an absolute Mayer sum.
- AP-like packets are the slow signed-convergence sector and need bounded
  core, Riesz-product, or cross-carrier pullback certificates.
- Therefore the polymer grammar should be typed by packet class and
  signed activity, not by raw support size or relation count.

=== Dirichlet / Schur sidecar network ===
